-- title:
--   Crossing lemma at a supersingular node of X₀(q) mod q
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $A$ a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $k$ a field of characteristic $q$, and $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ a ring homomorphism. Let $f$ lie in `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full modular function field of level $1\cdot q$ inside Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Assume (h₁) that $f$, as a Laurent series, lies in `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (1 * q) A.toSubring red`, the localisation of the modular ring of level $1\cdot q$ with $A$-integral coefficients at the kernel of $\mathrm{red}$, that (h₁F) its image under the reduction homomorphism `modularRedLocHom` lies in `modularFunctionFieldC k 1`, the subfield of Laurent series over $k$ generated by $k$ together with the two reduced $j$-expansions of level $1$, and that (h₁0) this image is nonzero; assume the same three conditions (h₂, h₂F, h₂0) for the image of $f$ under the Fricke involution `frickeInvolutionBar (1 * q)`. Let $a \in k$ lie in `ssJSet q k`, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has no nontrivial $k$-point killed by $q$, and assume $a^{q^2} = a$. Finally assume the support condition: for every place $W$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (a proper valuation subring containing $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ whose ring is a principal ideal ring) with $W.\mathrm{ord}\, f \ne 0$, it is not the case that simultaneously there is $x \in A$ with $\mathrm{red}\, x = a$ and $W.\mathrm{ord}(j - x) > 0$ and there is $y \in A$ with $\mathrm{red}\, y = a^q$ and $W.\mathrm{ord}(j_q - y) > 0$, where $j$ is the image of `jq` under the coefficient embedding and $j_q$ that of `qExpand ℚ (1 * q) jq`. Then there exists $c \in k$, $c \ne 0$, such that the place `(frobNodePair q a).1` $=$ `charLGeomPlaceOfPoint k a` takes the value $c$ at the reduction of $f$, and the place `(frobNodePair q a).2` $=$ `charLGeomPlaceOfPoint k (a ^ q)` takes the value $c$ at the reduction of the Fricke image of $f$; here a place $W$ takes value $c$ at $g$ when $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $W$ and the residue of $g$ equals the image of $c$ in the residue field.
--
--   This is the crossing lemma for the reduction of $X_0(q)$ modulo $q$, stated directly in the coordinates $(j, j_q)$ of a single supersingular node: a function which is a unit along both branches and none of whose zeros or poles specialises to the node $(a, a^q)$ has the same nonzero value on the two branches. It is used in the place-specialisation results [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.LevelOneProlongationPair.nodeValueLaw`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.LevelOneProlongationPair.nodeValueLaw), [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.exists_goodRep_gluedMk_eq_nodeUnit_smul_single_sub_self_levelOne`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.exists_goodRep_gluedMk_eq_nodeUnit_smul_single_sub_self_levelOne) and [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.exists_rep_reduce_notMem_of_moving_of_disjoint_levelOne`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.exists_rep_reduce_notMem_of_moving_of_disjoint_levelOne).
